  "basis": "calculated",
  "decisionGap": "A reader with a $1,850 benefit was told the 2027 Part B premium had not been announced and offered a $209.50 projection, so they could not see their net January 2027 deposit; CMS announced the final $209.40 on November 17, 2026.",
  "finding": "CMS set the 2027 standard Part B premium at $209.40, up $6.50 from $202.90, with a $292 deductible. A $1,850 benefit becomes $1,916.60 after the 3.6% COLA (SSA rounds down to the dime) and $1,707 net of the $209.40 premium (SSA rounds the payment down to the whole dollar).",
  "conditions": "Standard premium only; higher-income enrollees pay income-related adjustments and enter their own figure; SSA applies the COLA to the primary insurance amount so early-claim or family benefits can differ by cents; the COLA notice is exact.",
  "whatWouldChange": "IRMAA surcharges for higher-income enrollees; a different premium on the reader's notice; a correction of the CMS figure.",
